1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,500
Leather jacket. Three point four
trillion dollars.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,500
Jensen Huang built NVIDIA into the
world's most valuable company.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,000
Then he blew it up.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,500
First, he was caught with Alice Huang,
a Chinese executive

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,800
U.S. intelligence says
was a spy.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,500
Then, a second affair, with his
own VP who reported to him.

7
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:22,000
On November twelfth, after thirty
three years as CEO,

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,000
Jensen resigned.
Effective immediately.

9
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:25,400
The board didn't even fight it.

10
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,500
NVIDIA stock crashed fourteen
percent at the open.

11
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,500
It recovered to close down
four percent,

12
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,500
but the real damage?

13
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,000
One point six trillion dollars in
market value, wiped out over six weeks.

14
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,500
That's bigger than the
entire GDP of Australia.

15
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:42,500
AMD surged thirty percent
this week.

16
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,000
Broadcom jumped
twenty four percent.

17
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:47,500
But NVIDIA's partners
got crushed.

18
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:51,000
CoreWeave dropped seven percent,
and TSMC fell with it.

19
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:55,500
Analysts now value NVIDIA at two
twenty five per share without Jensen,

20
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,500
down from three hundred.

21
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:01,500
The new interim CEO, Colette Kress,
is a finance executive,

22
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,000
not an engineer.

23
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,500
And NVIDIA's earnings drop
November seventeenth.

24
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:11,500
Can anyone replace the man
in the leather jacket?

25
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:15,500
The bull case. NVIDIA is now at its
cheapest valuation in years,

26
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:17,500
and AI demand isn't slowing.

27
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:20,000
The bear case. No successor,

28
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,500
a spy scandal, and Congress
wants answers.

29
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:25,000
This is not financial advice.

30
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:28,000
Follow for more
finance breakdowns.

31
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,000
Drop a comment, who should be
NVIDIA's next CEO?
